\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell provided updates of activities conducted during Earth Month, including participation in community and school outreach events related to environmental awareness and sustainability education. Activities included participation in a tree planting event, \ldblquote Touch a Truck\rdblquote  events at local schools and City facilities, educational presentations regarding recycling and organics, and attendance at community events in coordination with City staff, volunteers, and community partners.\line\line Downtown Manhattan Beach Executive Director Kelly Stroman announced the opening of Coucou, a French bistro-style restaurant located at 1131 Manhattan Avenue, and noted that the restaurant would also be open for lunch on Mother\rquote s Day. She also announced the return of the \ldblquote Build the Bouquet\rdblquote  Mother\rquote s Day event in Downtown Manhattan Beach from 11:00 AM to 2:00 PM, during which participating businesses would distribute flowers and designated locations would provide bouquet wrapping materials for attendees.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Library Manager Cassandra Sargent announced that, in response to feedback from local teens, meeting rooms would be made available during the AP testing period as a study and gathering space from May 4, 2026, through May 14, 2026. The space would be available during afternoon hours and would include snacks, study space, and areas for students to collaborate and take breaks; and responded to City Council questions.\line\line Planning Manager Adam Finestone provided an update on the Project Pulse work effort related to the redevelopment of Parking Lot 3 and 400 Manhattan Beach Boulevard and noted that the year-long community visioning and outreach process, which began in August 2025, is currently past the halfway point. He also announced upcoming community workshops scheduled for Saturday, May 30, 2026, from 2:00 PM to 5:00 PM and Sunday, May 31, 2026, from 11:00 AM to 2:00 PM at the Joslyn Community Center, and stated that the workshops would include activities related to both properties and assist in developing conceptual project designs.\line\line Director of the Parents Softball Classic Dave Fratello announced the annual Parents Playing Against Parents softball tournament, a community fundraising event supporting the Mira Costa Girls Softball through MBX. The tournament involves parent teams from local schools and is scheduled for Sunday, May 31, 2026, and noted that most teams are formed, with additional participants still able to register. He also stated that this year marks the 20th anniversary of the tournament, which was founded in 2006 by Ross Kay and has been directed by the current organizer for the past 10 years. An afternoon ceremony is scheduled at approximately 3:00 PM prior to playoff games, and the event is open to the public.\cf2\i0\f1\fs24\par
}


