\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Interim Public Works Director Joseph DeFrancesco provided background on the item and introduced City Engineer Gilbert Gamboa who provided the PowerPoint presentation on the Proposed Five-Year Capital Improvements Program Fiscal Years 2027-2031.\line\line City Engineer Gamboa introduced Finance Director Libby Bretthauer who continued with the PowerPoint presentation on Senior and Scout House - Funding.\line\line City Engineer Gamboa continued with the PowerPoint presentation on the CIP Fund Funding Sources.\line\line\pard Finance Director Bretthauer and City Engineer Gamboa responded to City Council questions.\line\line Mayor Lesser noted that no members of the public were present to speak during public comment.\line\line\b The City Council directed staff to provide additional detail and analysis related to project costs and funding opportunities, including a more detailed breakout of soft costs and environmental cost projections; to evaluate whether bid data would provide a more accurate gauge of anticipated project costs and return with that information at the upcoming study session; to provide prioritization metrics and urgency assessments for potential deferred projects; to explore potential funding opportunities for pier renovations, including recently proposed federal legislation related to coastal pier improvements; to evaluate potential revenue-generating opportunities at the Scout House facility; to identify potential prior-year appropriations or other low-impact funding opportunities within Public Works projects that may be available for reallocation; and to evaluate potential refinancing or restructuring options related to existing debt obligations, including the Police/Fire Facility debt service, and return with associated fiscal impacts and opportunities for City Council consideration.\b0\line\line\cf1\i0\f1\fs24\par
